(10.5(1)) the forgiving (logistic) host: margin Delta needed to stay above the floor through the transient
   V6.1's transient: Delta=.08, 99% race: minimum 0.1397
   floor 0.2: Delta_min = 0.108
   floor 0.3: Delta_min = 0.165
   floor 0.5: Delta_min = 0.355
   (without the margin the logistic host dips below the floor and recovers: crossing is recoverable here, permanent on a threshold host)

(R1) long-run average liability vs cumulative advantage: tau(t) = nu - 1/(2 sqrt(t+1)) has average -> nu yet B(t) = sqrt(t+1)-1 -> infinity
   tau = nu (B=0): race share starts at 0.001; host stays above the floor
   tau = nu - 1/(2 sqrt(t+1)): race share starts at 0.001; host crosses the floor at t = 89
   both have long-run average liability nu: 'average at least nu' (with limsup) is necessary, not sufficient; the sharp necessary condition is that the cumulative advantage does not tend to infinity

